I have read that Valkyries have an advantage with cold resistance and
strength, so I decided to go dwarven to see if I could run the
protection racket with the minetown priest. It helps with surviving
the first few levels of the mines (due to the starting food rations
and +/- lamp) and allows to finish sokoban, but it wasn't as easy as I
thought.

Unfortunately, it wasn't that easy for me to avoid killing things on
the way to minetown ... especially when the downstairs to the mines
was DL3-4 and minetown was DL7-8. The few times I successfully ran the
racket I had YASDs ... and has anyone noticed that, if you save after
a promising game then restart it to play at a later time, you seem to
die right away after restarting??

1) I'd completed sokoban, got 2 BoH, found a shield of reflection but
elected not to use it to twoweapon, and some lieutenants in an unheard-
of display of AI teamwork got me with a ?oParalysis and a fire horn

2) I'd completed sokoban, got a BoH, a co-aligned altar, but was
blinded without telepathy and I got a white unicorn angry ... "It
kicks! It kicks! It butts! You die ..."

3) I'd completed sokoban, got a BoH, exploded it when I put in a bag
of tricks, was determined to make something of it despite ... and when
near death at the hands of a leocrotta, I tried to burn Elbereth with
a /oLightning ... apparently I mistyped it because the next turn I
died :P

4 & 5) Quafftesting potions and getting a ?oHallu, and making my pet
angry / making a shopkeeper angry

6) Chasing a nymph around in the mines because it had stolen my
shield, and falling into a pit with poisoned needles :P

This ascension was the toughest one so far.

* Highlights:

- failed protection racket attempt as I could not find the downstairs
to the mine for quite some time (I had apparently skipped the
passageway) ... didn't realize I missed the entrance until I got to
the Oracle and wondered, eh? What's going on?

- magic whistle found in shop. This with some level 6 spellbook that I
would have never comprehended anyway resulted in massive robbery of 3
general stores, which eventually funded -4 AC points, but all the
wandering around had resulted in leveling up to 11 (ugh)

- my cat running into a polymorph trap and turning into a baby purple
worm. They are slow (even when hasted) and are much less efficient at
looting stores. :P ... I tried to level it up to adult purple worm and
kept it for much of the pre-castle game but it eventually got pwned by
a white unicorn.

- making it down to the castle alive without reflection or magic
resistance.

- Fortunately, there was a silver dragon in the castle, who left me
scales.

- I had watched cdi use the drawbridge as a weapon, and had much grim
satisfaction figuring out the passtune and smashing the oncoming horde
(You hear smashing and crushing ... the foo falls into the moat ...
the foo is crushed by the portcullis! >=) ) ... thanks cdi

- I had found a scroll of charging earlier, so I used my wishes for a
cloak of magic resistance, gauntlets of power, a =oSD, a scroll of
genocide (for master mind flayers; I had previously genocided mind
flayers and intended not to genocide L's this time), another set of
gauntlets of power as I evaporated it read-testing a ?oDestroy Armor
[bonehead move], and finally for a scroll of charging for a magic
marker.

* Fun with rubber chickens

Previously, I had never wielded a 'trice corpse. Too dangerous and I
too timid. However, I made liberal use of them this game ... I had no
idea how fun they are. I thank someone at NAO whose game I was
watching - they taught me that I need to unwield it if I'm moving
around. Saved me another YASD.

- finding a rubber chicken in Baalzebub's lair ... and turning
Baalzebub into a statue

- finding another rubber chickatrice in Orcus' lair ... and turning
Orcus into a statue. (Incidentally, I had forgotten I had put my
skeleton key in my BoH and "a"pplied the same letter as my key - which
now referred to his wand of death. Argh).

- finding yet another rubber chicken just prior to Rodney ... and
turning him into a statue. (Incidentally, the original Rodney stole my
orb of fate ... and I did not realize I did not get it back until I
was like DL6 on the way up. No way I'm going back to DL42 again just
for that ... so I ended up buying another crystal ball in minetown, my
last visit, and writing a bunch of ?oGD with that magic marker)

- a final rubber chicken on the astral plane. The way to Tyr's altar
was littered with statues of angels and priests. Too bad death can't
be stoned.

* Near death experiences

- using a wand of create monster to generate fodder for sacrifices (I
really wanted Frost Brand or Grayswandir but ended up getting
snickersnee and Trollsbane (?!)) I generated a mind flayer. Since I
was a dumb dwarf, I hoped my intrinsic speed would allow me time to
get a /oLightning out of the bag and zap Elbereth. It did. Whew. It
escaped upstairs, so I repeated the process (getting lucky again) and
killed it from afar.

- two bones files (Mocoya and Ecker) that didn't really net me any
good loot, but Ecker's bones file was interesting because his ghost
and the gravestone were at the immediate entryway of a large 6x6 armor
store. The shopkeeper ?refused to step onto that square, so I thought
I might take advantage of that by walking out of the store with loot.

Well, apparently graves aren't enough to deter an angry pilfered
shopkeeper because he walked right over that on the way to burning me
up with (Eckers') wand of fire. Kops were blocking the exit corridor,
I was down to 17 hp, and I thought I was on the way to YASD
(especially after I tried to pay off all I had stolen ... with the $$
I had stolen from the other shopkeepers, and it said "Tirebolou is
after your hide!" ... but something happened and the Kops went away /
Tirebolou became peaceful again.

If that wasn't leaving well enough alone, when I became level 12,
gotten a pickaxe and fire resistance, somehow stupid me figured that
he wouldn't go back into his store because he was now on the other
side of the gravestone, so I walled off one end with a ?oEarth and
pickaxed my way through the other side of the shop. What was I
thinking?? There he was again, angry ... and no way to pay him off
this time because I hadn't stolen anything. Thankfully I was fast, so
I got one square distance, and walled him off again with another ?
oEarth (thank you Sokoban!) but not before I had gotten to 40 hp /
138.

Determined to loot the shop, I tried once more much later, but by that
time had most of my ascension kit, so I ended up just losing my
telepathy and having to regain it by finding an eye in the mines.

All in all, interesting asides and near-deaths, but not very
contributory to my ascensions. Moloch's sanctum was DL 52 which I
believe is the deepest it can be. Fun fun. Also my first ascension
without being crowned. Or having teleport / teleport control. Liches'
summon nasties is really not so bad if they can't summon mind flayers,
and they can be killed easily if you occupy the upstair.

